{:edb/db-before-t 1607 :edb/db-after-t 1608 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534920 50 #inst "2026-10-08T11:02:07.905Z" 13194139534920 true] [17592186100604 1100 "Let\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/5357fcb0ec150699b4d50cbd6fa9651c421ac3500660703396146362160328a2.png)\nand\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/63d354773d145f05e73e808efe2a21164cb28d6ff19ae104d6bbde6510cf10e6.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" 13194139534920 true] [17592186100604 1100 "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" 13194139534920 false] [17592186100606 1100 "Let\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/035755bae569c8c9323112891f959076dd727d3ef40ba66c6c40dadf5ddc8f84.png)\nand\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043361/assets/e53c9ba3bb64b81e44f8f4f49ac77408b7db6ee458be3d43b687d9ed8897ad59.png)\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" 13194139534920 true] [17592186100606 1100 "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" 13194139534920 false] [17592186100782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319926 13194139534920 true] [17592186100782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319962 13194139534920 true] [17592186100782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319969 13194139534920 true] [17592186100783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319944 13194139534920 true] [17592186100783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319976 13194139534920 true] [17592186100783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319983 13194139534920 true] [17592186100783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319990 13194139534920 true] [17592186100784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319939 13194139534920 true] [17592186100784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319950 13194139534920 true] [17592186100784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186319956 13194139534920 true] [17592186101235 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534920 true] [17592186101235 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\n- The product $AB$ is well defined\n- The product $BA$ is well defined\n- The product $AC$ is well defined" 13194139534920 true] [17592186101235 1100 "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $A, B$, and $C$?\n\n1. The product $AB$ is well defined\n2. The product $BA$ is well defined\n3. The product $AC$ is well defined" 13194139534920 false] [17592186101235 1145 "Notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{A}_{3\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 1}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false." 13194139534920 true] [17592186101237 1017 #edb/ref 17592186099159 13194139534920 false] [17592186101237 1017 #edb/ref 17592186319933 13194139534920 true] [17592186101237 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534920 true] [17592186101237 1100 "Let\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$.\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA$?" 13194139534920 false] [17592186101237 1100 "Let\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" 13194139534920 true] [17592186101237 1145 "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={BA}_{2\\times 2}\n$$" 13194139534920 true] [17592186101317 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534920 true] [17592186101317 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -0 & 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statement are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\n- The product $AB$ is well defined\n- The product $BA$ is well defined\n- The product $AC$ is well defined" 13194139534920 true] [17592186101317 1100 "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ -0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$,\n\nWhich of the following statement are true regarding the matrices $A, B$, and $C$?\n\n1. The product $AB$ is well defined\n2. The product $BA$ is well defined\n3. The product $AC$ is well defined" 13194139534920 false] [17592186101317 1145 "Notice that $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that all three statements are true." 13194139534920 true] [17592186319926 1017 #edb/ref 17592186319927 13194139534920 true] [17592186319926 1089 "q-22056" 13194139534920 true] [17592186319926 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534920 true] [17592186319926 1100 "$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $R,S,$ and $T?$\n\n- The product $SR$ is well defined\n- The product $RS$ is well defined\n- The product $ST$ is well defined" 13194139534920 true] [17592186319926 1113 #uuid "960a6f14-6ea1-5d58-9c80-cf93ecc61484" 13194139534920 true] [17592186319926 1145 "Notice that $R$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $S$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $T$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $R$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $S$ and $3$ rows in $T.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $T,$ the matrices $S$ and $T$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{T}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false." 13194139534920 true] [17592186319927 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319928 13194139534920 true] [17592186319927 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319929 13194139534920 true] [17592186319927 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319930 13194139534920 true] [17592186319927 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319931 13194139534920 true] [17592186319927 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319932 13194139534920 true] [17592186319927 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534920 true] [17592186319927 1041 "selection" 13194139534920 true] [17592186319927 1104 #edb/ref 17592186319931 13194139